  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Public-Private Partnership development Ghana</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to form a public-private partnership (PPP) with partners that commit to contributing collectively to the ambition of the combi-track Horti Ghana, a vibrant and sustainable horti sector. The PPP will be driven by the Dutch private sector in close collaboration with Ghanaian stakeholders, and will be based on commercial opportunities for participants. The PPP will focus on the seed sector, but can also include partners in the broader value chain, e.g. in inputs and processing. This project will identify interested and relevant actors in the Dutch private sector, connect them to Ghanaian stakeholders and support the development of a Quick Scan for a proposal for collective action. It will connect the PPP to ongoing initiatives such as ACHI and Grains for Growth and identify how these initiatives can facilitate the endeavours of the PPP in Ghana.</narrative>
  </description>
